<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 1500 CST, USDA said. Boxed beef uneven on mostly moderate demand and offerings. Select and Choice round cuts lower, rib cuts weak, chuck cuts uneven and loin cuts steady.</p>
<p>Beef trimmings not established.</p>
<p>269 Fab Lds   CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>    50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>31 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     103.30	102.70	 97.81	 97.11</p>
<p>		   -0.40	 -0.32	 -0.03	 -0.34</p>
<p>Rib	  152.13	150.37	145.12	142.95</p>
<p>Chuck	 68.68	 66.36	 68.63	 65.67</p>
<p>Round	 90.33	 90.33	 88.73	 88.73</p>
<p>Loin	 170.97	172.29	150.59	152.54</p>
<p>Brisket     61.17	 61.17	 61.71	 61.71</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  65.35	 65.28	 65.58	 65.42</p>
<p>Flank	 56.19	 56.19	 54.13	 54.13</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
